    "text": "To understand it, we have to go back to July nineteen forty four. The second World War is still raging, but delegates from forty four Allied nations gather at a hotel in the mountains of New Hampshire, in a small town called Bretton Woods. Their job is to design the money system for the world after the war, and America walks in holding almost every card. Its factories are untouched, Europe is in ruins, and the United States holds roughly two thirds of all the gold in the world's central banks.",
